The butler is picking up the curtain rod.

Quinn: Now I've been wondering, my Lord, what is it you were doing back before
you ran for office?

Vespertilion: This America, your America...my America...it truly is the land of
opportunity. In the Old Country, I was nothing. A mere municipal authority
commissioner. But here...here, I can be so much more.

[============================================================================]

The butler is moving from the trophy room to the granite-gilded passage.

Vespertilion: It took decades, but now I have risen to become a Count...and
perhaps this is only the beginning. Who knows how many decades it might take?
But one day I might be an assemblyman, or even a state legislator! Imagine the
votes of all of New York, the authority of the state’s population, vested in
me, a single individual.

[============================================================================]

The butler is moving from the granite-gilded passage to the chapel.

Vespertilion: The power to vote on bills, or introduce amendments! That is a
power beyond wealth, beyond fame. And with the power will come the lobbyists.
The PACs. The campaign contributions. Is this not your American Dream? That a
mere municipal authority commissioner from a minor noble family could one day
hold a seat in a federated state legislature?

Quinn: I’ll drink to that!

